---
import AboutHeroImage from "../assets/blog-placeholder-about.jpg";
import Profile_zosia from "../assets/zosia_profile.jpg";
import Profile_maude from "../assets/maude_profile.jpg";
import Profile_keira from "../assets/keira_profile.jpg";
import Profile_charlie_wilcoxon from "../assets/Charlie_Wilcoxon_profile.jpg";
import Profile_charlie_miller from "../assets/Charlie_Miller_profile.jpg";
import Profile_bridget from "../assets/Bridget_Noonan_profile.jpg";
import Profile_gianna from "../assets/Gianna_DeBono_profile.jpg";
import Profile_william from "../assets/William_Thissell_profile.jpg";
import Profile_paul from "../assets/Paul_Didenko_profile.jpg";
import Profile_nick from "../assets/Nick_Cecil_Profile.jpg.jpeg";
import Profile_jack from "../assets/Jack_Perry_Profile_pic.png";
import Profile_brennan from "../assets/brennan_profile_pic_v2.jpg";
import Profile_joseph from "../assets/Joseph_Calabrese_Profile_pic.png";
import Profile_jennie_kate from "../assets/Jennie_Kate_Hannis_Profile_pic.png";
import Profile_khoa from "../assets/Khoa_Nguyen_Profile_pic.png";
import Profile_sofia from "../assets/Sofia_Pudner_Profile_pic.png";
import Profile_victor from "../assets/Victor_Paltineanu_Profile_pic.png";
import Layout from "../layouts/BlogPost.astro";
---

<Layout
	title="Founding Charter"
	description="Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet"
	author=""
	pubDate={new Date("March 22 2026")}
	heroImage={AboutHeroImage}
>

	<p>
		The Arena Journal is an intellectual publication rooted in conservatism
		and founded to bring the intellectual rigor and vibrancy of conservative
		life at the University of Virginia to the published page. It exists as a
		platform for UVA undergraduates, especially those struggling to find
		opportunities for intellectual engagement in a culture of general
		intellectual fear and apathy, to write seriously and thoughtfully about
		politics, philosophy, economics, literature, or any other intellectual
		discipline. Throughout the publication process, which includes writing
		workshops and colloquia, our members and contributors engage with
		precision both in the ongoing conversations surrounding them and with
		each other. Each publication is not merely a thoughtful collection of
		articles, but evidence of vivacious intellectual discourse and formation
		that preserves a culture of charity, rigor, and courage among
		conservatives at UVA.
	</p>
	<div class="arena-section-heading">
		<h3>Our Executive Team</h3>
	</div>
	<div class="card">
		<img src={Profile_zosia.src} alt="Profile Photo" class="card-image" />
		<div class="card-text">
			<p>
				<b>Zosia Collins, Co-Editor-in-Chief</b><br />Zosia is a second
				year at UVA, where she is pursuing a degree in the
				extraordinarily practical field of Classics. Besides editing The
				Arena, she is an intern at the Institute for Family Studies, a
				fellow at the Blue Ridge Center, and highly involved with
				Catholic Hoos. Although a very busy person, she will make time
				for anyone who wishes to discuss flute music, good literature,
				writing novels, or ancient philosophy.
			</p>
		</div>
		<img
			src={Profile_charlie_wilcoxon.src}
			alt="Profile Photo"
			class="card-image"
		/>
		<div class="card-text">
			<p>
				<b>Charles Wilcoxon, Co-Editor-in-Chief</b><br />Coming from
				Columbus, Ohio, Charles is a second-year student at UVA studying
				history. He is involved in the altar service and parish
				maintenance ministries with Catholic Hoos, and, alongside Mr.
				Miller and Miss DeBono, he is a founder of CREDO Apologetics. Be
				careful getting into conversations with him about history,
				philosophy, literature, film, or economics —you might be there
				for a while. Especially dangerous, however, is picking his brain
				on Star Wars and Lord of the Rings.
			</p>
		</div>
		<img src={Profile_maude.src} alt="Profile Photo" class="card-image" />
		<div class="card-text">
			<p>
				<b>Pamella Parker, Editor and Contributor</b><br />Pamella is a
				second year Chemistry major at UVA. You may know her better by
				her middle name, Maude. She still doesn’t know what her parents
				were thinking. She’s known for her sharp sense of humor,
				practical mindset, and ability to keep things both thoughtful
				and down-to-earth. She’ll talk your ear off about anything, and
				whatever her opinion may be, it will certainly be a strong one!
			</p>
		</div>
		<img src={Profile_keira.src} alt="Profile Photo" class="card-image" />
		<div class="card-text">
			<p>
				<b>Keira Thomas, Social Media Manager and Contributor</b><br
				/>Originally from Front Royal VA, Keira is a second year at UVA,
				majoring in History and English. An aspiring teacher, Keira
				loves to discuss literature and humanities as a way to engage
				with the good, the true, and the beautiful. At UVA, she is
				involved with Catholic Hoos and handles events coordination for
				Hoos for Life, in addition to contributing to the Arena.
			</p>
		</div>
		<img src={Profile_victor.src} alt="Profile Photo" class="card-image" />
		<div class="card-text">
			<p>
				<b>Victor Paltineanu, Chief Strategy Officer</b><br />Hailing from Bucharest, Romania, 
				Victor is a second-year student at the University of Virginia studying Foreign Affairs. 
				On Grounds, he serves as External Affairs Chair for the National 
				Security, Intelligence, and Defense (NSID) Club and works as a Language 
				Consultant for VISAS, teaching English to Japanese and Korean graduate 
				students at UVA Law. Outside of his academic and extracurricular pursuits, 
				he enjoys traveling and exploring his interests in politics, film and 
				television, history, literature, and Formula 1. Pursue these topics at your 
				own discretion. 
			</p>
		</div>
		<img src={Profile_jack.src} alt="Profile Photo" class="card-image" />
		<div class="card-text">
			<p>
				<b>Jack Perry, Outreach Chair</b><br />Jack is a second year 
				at UVA from Reston, Virginia, majoring in Economics with a minor 
				in German. He is involved with the Catholic Hoos Homeless Ministry 
				and is active in College Republicans. In his free time, he enjoys 
				reading, lifting, fishing, hiking, and a good chess match.  
			</p>
		</div>
		<img src={Profile_jennie_kate.src} alt="Profile Photo" class="card-image" />
		<div class="card-text">
			<p>
				<b>Jennie-Kate Hannis, Design Chair</b><br />Jennie-Kate is a 
				first-year student from Round Hill, VA planning to major in History 
				and Government. She also has interests in journalism and community 
				service. In her free time, Jennie-Kate enjoys reading, watching and 
				discussing films, and baking.   
			</p>
		</div>
		<img src={Profile_sofia.src} alt="Profile Photo" class="card-image" />
		<div class="card-text">
			<p>
				<b>Sofia Pudner, Fidelity Chair</b><br />Hailing from Richmond, 
				Virginia, Sofia is a first-year student at UVA exploring her interests 
				in economics, finance, and the humanities. She is involved in Catholic 
				Hoos, Smart Women Securities, and the Women in Economics Club, and she 
				is always looking for new ways to get involved around Grounds. Outside 
				of class, she enjoys spending time with friends, reading, writing, and 
				talking about just about anything. A big fan of Shakespeare, she loves 
				to talk about both his plays and their more modern movie adaptations.    
			</p>
		</div>
		<img src={Profile_nick.src} alt="Profile Photo" class="card-image" />
		<div class="card-text">
			<p>
				<b>Nick Cecil, Technology Chair</b><br />Nick is a second-year at UVA 
				from Arlington, Virginia, studying Economics, Statistics, and Data Science.
				Aside from being involved with Catholic Hoos, he also enjoys guitar, hiking, 
				reading, lifting, food, and plays way too many intramural sports.
			</p>
		</div>
		<img src={Profile_brennan.src} alt="Profile Photo" class="card-image" />
		<div class="card-text">
			<p>
				<b>Brennan Shea, Technology Associate</b><br />Hailing from Chesterfield, 
				Virginia, Brennan is a first-year at UVA. In his free time, he loves 
				playing guitar, pursuing personal coding projects, and playing a variety 
				of sports ranging from soccer to ultimate frisbee. He is also involved in 
				the altar-service community with Catholic Hoos, and if he’s doing homework, 
				chances are it’s in the Catholic Hoos Common Room. 
			</p>
		</div>
		<img src={Profile_paul.src} alt="Profile Photo" class="card-image" />
		<div class="card-text">
			<p>
				<b>Paul Didenko, Journal Photographer</b><br />Paul Didenko is a
				second-year from Sevierville, Tennessee, studying Mechanical
				Engineering. He is involved in the choir and instrumentalists at
				Catholic Hoos and dabbles in the realm of photography.
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
	<div class="arena-section-heading">
		<h3>Our Contributors</h3>
	</div>
	<div class="card">
		<img
			src={Profile_charlie_miller.src}
			alt="Profile Photo"
			class="card-image"
		/>
		<div class="card-text">
			<p>
				<b>Charles Miller</b><br />Charlie is a
				second-year at UVA from Richmond VA planning on majoring in
				Economics and Finance. He is involved in the altar service and
				men's ministries with Catholic Hoos, and is the founder of the
				CREDO Apologetics club. He enjoys playing table tennis,
				spikeball, chess, poker, basketball, pool and guitar. He enjoys
				discussing philosophy and theology particularly in the realms of
				Catholic apologetics.
			</p>
		</div>
		<img src={Profile_bridget.src} alt="Profile Photo" class="card-image" />
		<div class="card-text">
			<p>
				<b>Bridget Noonan</b><br />Bridget is a
				second-year at the University of Virginia planning to study
				Politics and Economics. She is currently involved at UVA as the
				Finance Chair for A Moment of Magic, as the Website Manager for
				Catholic Hoos, and as an active member of Undergraduate
				Constitutional Law and Hoos For Life. Bridget enjoys deep
				conversations about subjects that pique her interest and
				particularly always loves to discuss political theory and
				philosophy or literature and film reviews.
			</p>
		</div>
		<img src={Profile_william.src} alt="Profile Photo" class="card-image" />
		<div class="card-text">
			<p>
				<b>William Thissell</b><br />Growing up in
				Alexandria, Virginia, William is a second-year student at UVA
				studying Aerospace Engineering. He is involved in Catholic Hoos
				and UVA Rocketry, where he is on the airbreaks team. He loves
				spending time outdoors and tries his luck at the poker tables
				every now and then.
			</p>
		</div>
		<img src={Profile_gianna.src} alt="Profile Photo" class="card-image" />
		<div class="card-text">
			<p>
				<b>Gianna DeBono</b><br />Gianna is a
				second-year from Greenwich, CT, interested in majoring in
				Political Philosophy, Policy and Law. She has a big love for
				music and is a member of the Virginia Belles, a Capella group
				here on grounds. She’s also a fan of philosophy and politics and
				is in the Jefferson Literary and Debate Society. She plays
				intramural soccer in her free time and is involved with Catholic
				Hoos on their service council and the CREDO Apologetics group.
			</p>
		</div>
		<img src={Profile_joseph.src} alt="Profile Photo" class="card-image" />
		<div class="card-text">
			<p>
				<b>Joseph Calabrese</b><br />Joseph is a 
				fourth-year UVA student from New Jersey dual majoring in History 
				and Foreign Affairs. He is the head altar-server for Catholic Hoos 
				and is highly involved in St. Thomas Aquinas Church. He enjoys 
				watching movies, playing golf, and fancies himself an amateur sommelier. 
			</p>
		</div>
		<img src={Profile_khoa.src} alt="Profile Photo" class="card-image" />
		<div class="card-text">
			<p>
				<b>Khoa Nguyen</b><br />Hailing from Springfield, Virginia, Khoa Nguyen 
				is a second-year student at the University of Virginia in the College of
				Arts and Sciences. He does not know his major yet, but he is considering 
				studying either Cognitive Science or Mathematics. Outside of classes, 
				he is involved with Catholic Hoos and its homeless ministry, the Center 
				for Christian Study, and Theological Horizons. You will often find him 
				writing short stories, playing guitar, reading, or taking a good walk.  
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
	<style>
		.arena-pullquote {
			margin: 2rem auto;
			max-width: 42rem;
			padding: 1.5rem 0 1.5rem 1.5rem;
			border-left: 3px solid var(--color-oxblood, #6e1423);
			font-style: italic;
			font-size: 1.1rem;
			line-height: 1.6;
			color: var(--color-ink-soft, inherit);
		}
		.arena-pullquote cite {
			display: block;
			margin-top: 1rem;
			font-style: normal;
			font-size: 0.8rem;
			letter-spacing: 0.15em;
			text-transform: uppercase;
			color: var(--color-oxblood, inherit);
			opacity: 0.85;
		}
		.arena-section-heading {
			display: flex;
			align-items: baseline;
			gap: 0.85rem;
			margin: 2.5rem 0 1.75rem;
		}
		.arena-section-heading::after {
			content: "";
			flex: 1 1 auto;
			height: 1px;
			background: var(--color-oxblood, #6e1423);
		}
		.arena-section-heading h3 {
			margin: 0;
			font-size: 0.85rem;
			letter-spacing: 0.2em;
			text-transform: uppercase;
			color: var(--color-oxblood, inherit);
			white-space: nowrap;
		}
		.card {
			display: grid;
			grid-template-columns: 1fr; /* single column on mobile */
			gap: 0.6rem;
			align-items: center;
		}
		.card-image {
			width: 200px;
			height: 200px;
			border-radius: 50%;
			object-fit: cover;
			justify-self: center;
			border: 1px solid var(--color-line, #d6d2c8);
		}
		@media (min-width: 640px) {
			.card {
				grid-template-columns: 250px 1fr; /* fixed image width + fluid text */
			}
		}
	</style>
</Layout>
